{"metadata":{"externalID":"s:4GLib8testFailyyF","role":"symbol","title":"testFail()","modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"testFail","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"symbolKind":"func","roleHeading":"Function"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/testFail()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Indicates that a test failed."}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/testfail()"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"testFail"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This function can be called multiple times from the same test.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"You can use this function if your test failed in a recoverable way.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Do not use this function if the failure of a test could cause"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"other tests to malfunction."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Calling this function will not stop the test from running, you"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"need to return from the test function yourself. So you can"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"produce additional diagnostic messages or even continue running","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the test."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If not called from inside a test, this function does nothing."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Note that unlike [func","type":"text"},{"code":"GLib.test_skip","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] and [func"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.test_incomplete"},{"text":"],","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this function does not log a message alongside the test failure.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"If details of the test failure are available, either log them with","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"[func"},{"code":"GLib.test_message","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] before [func"},{"code":"GLib.test_fail","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"], or use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[func","type":"text"},{"code":"GLib.test_fail_printf","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] instead."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/testFail()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Indicates that a test failed."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/testFail()","title":"testFail()","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/testfail()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"testFail"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib","title":"GLib","abstract":[],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/glib","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"}}}